{title: Through the Night of Doubt and Sorrow}
{artist: Bernhardt S. Ingemann, tr. Sabine Baring-Gould / Henry T. Smart}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Closing}
{key: A}
{tempo: 92}
{time: 4/4}
{score: through-the-night-of-doubt-and-sorrow.abc}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Open Hymnal score (Through_The_Night_of_Doubt_and_Sorrow-Rex_Gloriae)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[A]Through the [F#m]night [E]of [A]doubt and [E]sorrow
[A]On[F#m]ward [Bm]goes the [E]pilgrim [A]band,
[A]Sing[E]ing [A]songs of [F#m]expec[B7]tation,
[B7]Marching [C#m]to the pro[B]mised [E]land.
[E]Clear before [Bm]us [A]through [E]the dark[A]ness
[F#m]Gleams [E]and [A]burns the [E7]gui[A]ding [E]light:
[A]Bro[E]ther [A]clasps the hand of [E]brother,
[A]Step[F#m]ping [D]fear[A]less [E]through the [A]night.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[A]One the [F#m]light [E]of [A]God’s own [E]presence,
[A]O’er [F#m]His [Bm]ransomed [E]people [A]shed,
[A]Cha[E]sing [A]far the [F#m]gloom and [B7]terror,
[B7]Brightening [C#m]all the path [B]we [E]tread:
[E]One the ob[Bm]ject [A]of [E]our jour[A]ney,
[F#m]One [E]the [A]faith which [E7]nev[A]er [E]tires,
[A]One [E]the [A]earnest looking [E]forward,
[A]One [F#m]the [D]hope [A]our [E]God in[A]spires.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[A]One the [F#m]strain [E]that [A]lips of [E]thousands
[A]Lift [F#m]as [Bm]from the [E]heart of [A]one;
[A]One [E]the [A]conflict, [F#m]one the [B7]peril
[B7]One the [C#m]march in God [B]be[E]gun:
[E]One the glad[Bm]ness [A]of [E]rejoi[A]cing
[F#m]On [E]the [A]far e[E7]ter[A]nal [E]shore,
[A]Where [E]the [A]one almighty [E]Father
[A]Reigns [F#m]in [D]love [A]for [E]ever[A]more.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[A]Onward, [F#m]there[E]fore, [A]pilgrim [E]brothers,
[A]On[F#m]ward, [Bm]with the [E]cross our [A]aid!
[A]Bear [E]its [A]shame, and [F#m]fight its [B7]battle,
[B7]Till we [C#m]rest beneath [B]its [E]shade.
[E]Soon shall come [Bm]the [A]great [E]awak[A]ing,
[F#m]Soon [E]the [A]rending [E7]of [A]the [E]tomb;
[A]Then [E]the [A]scattering of all [E]shadows,
[A]And [F#m]the [D]end [A]of [E]toil and [A]gloom.
{end_of_verse}
